Package: pocketlens
Version: @VERSION@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: adb | android-tools-adb, v4l2loopback-dkms, libgl1, libegl1, libfontconfig1, libxkbcommon0, libdbus-1-3, libxcb-cursor0, policykit-1 | pkexec
Recommends: pipewire-bin, v4l-utils
Suggests: ffmpeg, python3
Maintainer: PocketLens <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/CamiloFerreira/pocketlens
Description: Android phone as webcam and microphone
 PocketLens turns an Android phone running the PocketLens app into a
 virtual webcam (v4l2loopback, "Android Cam") and microphone (PipeWire,
 "Android Mic") over USB (adb) or Wi-Fi.
 .
 Includes the desktop client (pocketlens) and a headless command line
 tool (pocketlens-cli, needs ffmpeg). The phone app (APK) is bundled and
 can be installed over USB from the client.
